menu "EPSolar Zigbee sensor"

config EPSOLAR_UPDATE_INTERVAL_SECONDS
    int "Telemetry update interval (seconds)"
    range 1 86400
    default 60
    help
        Time between Modbus reads and Zigbee attribute updates.

config EPSOLAR_ZIGBEE_KEEP_ALIVE_MS
    int "Sleepy end device long poll interval (milliseconds)"
    range 1000 3600000
    default 60000
    help
        How often the node polls its parent when it is not fast polling.

        The workaround circulating for espressif/esp-zigbee-sdk#782 is to set
        this extremely high - one hour - which delays whatever it is about the
        long poll firing that wedges the device into permanent fast poll. It is
        offered here so that can be tested, but note that this node is not the
        idle device in that report: it transmits every telemetry cycle, and its
        own traffic starts fast poll regardless of this value.

        The end device timeout is derived from this automatically. A parent ages
        a child out after that timeout without a keepalive poll, so a long poll
        interval that outlasts it loses the node entirely - which is the trap in
        raising this value on its own.

config EPSOLAR_ZIGBEE_FAST_POLL_MS
    int "Sleepy end device fast poll interval (milliseconds)"
    range 100 7000
    default 1000
    help
        How often the node polls its parent while fast polling. The library
        defaults this to 200 ms and never falls back to the long poll interval,
        so in practice this sets the idle wake rate: two wakes per interval,
        indefinitely.

        The range is not arbitrary. A parent discards an indirect transaction
        after macTransactionPersistenceTime, 7.68 s, so any value at or beyond
        that guarantees the APS ack is destroyed before the node arrives to
        collect it, and every report comes back 0xa7. The APS layer's own ack
        wait is shorter still and is the real ceiling, but its value in this
        stack is unverified.

        The only interval known to deliver acks on this node is the 200 ms
        default. Walk this up one step at a time and watch probe_ok against
        probe_fail in the cycle line; back off as soon as failures appear.

config EPSOLAR_LIGHT_SLEEP
    bool "Enable automatic light sleep"
    depends on PM_ENABLE && FREERTOS_USE_TICKLESS_IDLE
    default y
    help
        Sleep between telemetry cycles. The Zigbee stack and the Modbus
        transactions hold the chip awake whenever they need it, so this only
        covers genuinely idle time. The firmware checks for a USB host once
        at boot and keeps light sleep off for that whole run when one is
        present: USB Serial JTAG does not survive a light sleep, and the USJ
        connection monitor's own no-light-sleep lock is not reliable at
        1000 Hz ticks. Turn this off outright to force the same no-sleep
        reference behaviour on battery as well.

config EPSOLAR_MODBUS_UART_PORT
    int "Modbus UART port"
    range 0 1
    default 1
    help
        UART0 and UART1 are the ESP32-C6 high-performance UARTs. UART1 is
        used by default so USB Serial/JTAG remains available for logs.

config EPSOLAR_MODBUS_TX_GPIO
    int "Modbus UART TX GPIO"
    range 0 30
    default 16
    help
        XIAO D6, labelled TX.

config EPSOLAR_MODBUS_RX_GPIO
    int "Modbus UART RX GPIO"
    range 0 30
    default 17
    help
        XIAO D7, labelled RX.

config EPSOLAR_MODBUS_BAUD_RATE
    int "Modbus baud rate"
    range 1200 115200
    default 115200

config EPSOLAR_MODBUS_SLAVE_ADDRESS
    int "Modbus slave address"
    range 1 247
    default 1

endmenu
